s. Turn them off for sparklines or when the surrounding UI already names the values."],[1556,"\\`xNice\\` and \\`yNice\\` round the domain out to friendlier numbers (e.g. 0.2 to 1.0), so ticks land on values people expect."],[1559,"\\`xPaddingOuter\\` and \\`yPaddingOuter\\` add breathing room at the ends of a band or point scale so the first and last values are not pinned to the edges."],[1419,"\\`xTickFormat\\` and \\`yTickFormat\\` shape the axis labels - abbreviated dates on one axis, thousands separators on the other. The functions receive the raw accessor value, so they also cover currency, units, or percentages."],[1552,"\\`xTickFormat\\` and \\`yTickFormat\\` shape the axis labels - dates, currency, units, percentages - and the tooltip follows the same formatting."],[1549,"\\`xTickMarks\\` and \\`yTickMarks\\` draw the short lines at each tick value, which helps tie a label to its exact position on the axis."],[1547,"\\`xTitle\\` and \\`yTitle\\` label what each axis actually measures, e.g. \"Month\" and \"Temperature (°F)\"."],[1557,"\\`xZero\\` and \\`yZero\\` stretch the domain to include zero. Worth doing when the absolute size of the values matters, not just their movement."],[1165,"`--color-input-background-default`"],[1162,"`--color-input-background-selected`"],[1171,"`--color-input-text-default`"],[1172,"`--ux-1glcx6s`"],[1160,"`--ux-1m9ys0v`"],[1166,"`--ux-1nu8itt`"],[1169,"`--ux-1sbfig8`"],[1163,"`--ux-sywk25`"],[1175,"`--ux-zvaw3s`"],[456,"`[data-disabled]`"],[460,"`[data-focused]`"],[458,"`[data-invalid]`"],[154,"`@godaddy/antares/date` re-exports `@internationalized/date`, the package behind these date primitives."],[312,"`@godaddy/antares/date` re-exports `@internationalized/date`, the package behind these date primitives. Locale comes from a host `<I18nProvider>`. This version has no typed/segmented entry - selection is via the calendar."],[1649,"`<Box blockAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[1651,"`<Box inlineAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[1645,"`<B